import{_ as t,o as i,c as n,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 260 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Comparison With Ye Fan: Differences Between Oligarchic and Bestowal Styles","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 260 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Comparison With Ye Fan: Differences Between Oligarchic and Bestowal Styles","no":260,"module":2,"tags":["Tang-Luo","Ye Fan","Cover the Sky","Oligarchic","Bestowal","Myriad-Realms Benchmark"],"related":["30-Five Symbiotic Civilization Typology Overview","29-Symbiosis Degree Evaluation System","17-Plane Transcendent Standards"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0260_模块2-唐罗-叶凡对比篇.md","filePath":"en/0260_模块2-唐罗-叶凡对比篇.md"}'),a={name:"en/0260_模块2-唐罗-叶凡对比篇.md"};function s(r,e,l,h,c,d){return i(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-260-tang-luo-decomposition-comparison-with-ye-fan-differences-between-oligarchic-and-bestowal-styles" tabindex="-1">Entry 260 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Comparison With Ye Fan: Differences Between Oligarchic and Bestowal Styles <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-260-tang-luo-decomposition-comparison-with-ye-fan-differences-between-oligarchic-and-bestowal-styles" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 260 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Comparison With Ye Fan: Differences Between Oligarchic and Bestowal Styles&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Tang-Luo System (Entry 10)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-give-all-beings-a-road-or-give-the-ye-family-ten-thousand-years-of-peace" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Give all beings a road, or give the Ye family ten thousand years of peace <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-give-all-beings-a-road-or-give-the-ye-family-ten-thousand-years-of-peace" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Give all beings a road, or give the Ye family ten thousand years of peace&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the law-first axiom requires order to be written into laws, not into a family. Ye Fan (Cover the Sky) and Tang Luo, one is the oligarchic specimen, the other the bestowal specimen. This entry takes the law-first axiom as core, comparing the two tiers&#39; structural differences. Protagonist uniqueness dependency: Tang Luo = high (bestowal style), Ye Fan = medium (oligarchic style). The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Ye Fan system&#39;s waste</strong>: Cover the Sky&#39;s &quot;ten-thousand-year peace&quot; bears the surname Ye — order after Great Emperor and Mortal-World Immortal is essentially co-rule by Ye Fan and his close circle of friends. Energy is concentrated in a small circle; all beings outside the circle are merely &quot;protected,&quot; with no participation right</li><li><strong>Tang Luo system&#39;s waste</strong>: energy is concentrated in Tang Luo alone, the circle smaller than Ye Fan&#39;s, but at least the entry is open to all humanity</li></ul><p>Comparison points: Ye Fan&#39;s waste is <strong>circularization</strong> — a few strong ones co-rule, civilization&#39;s dividends distributed by circle; Tang Luo&#39;s waste is <strong>single-pointization</strong> — one person decides, the circle is small but the door is open. By &quot;open radius,&quot; Tang Luo is actually wider than Ye Fan; by &quot;institutional stability,&quot; Ye Fan&#39;s oligarchic group is slightly more stable than Tang Luo&#39;s single point — more people, slightly higher fault tolerance.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Ye Fan system&#39;s regression</strong>: oligarchic co-rule depends on &quot;brothers of one mind.&quot; When the first generation of Great Emperors is alive, ten-thousand-year peace; when the first generation ages, does the second generation still have this vision? History repeatedly proves oligarchic groups&#39; second and third generations inevitably infight. Cover the Sky&#39;s late realm collapse is precisely oligarchic structure unable to hold up the plot</li><li><strong>Tang Luo system&#39;s regression</strong>: single-point dependency, Tang Luo retires and it slowly regresses. But the academies and method organizations he left are more operable than the &quot;brotherly loyalty&quot; Ye Fan left — loyalty is not heritable, schools can be transmitted</li></ul><p>Regression rhythm: Ye Fan group is <strong>group corruption</strong> (each generation worse), Tang Luo group is <strong>single-point decay</strong> (slowly cools after one person leaves). Both regressions are regression, only the form differs.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Ye Fan&#39;s predation</strong>: the subject of &quot;ten-thousand-year peace&quot; is the Ye family; all beings are only beneficiaries of peace, not peace&#39;s legislators. The predation form is <strong>patriciate-style</strong> — civilizational leadership solidified in one strong family / group&#39;s hand</li><li><strong>Tang Luo&#39;s predation</strong>: bestowal style, the subject is Tang Luo personally, all beings are recipients. The predation form is softer, but the essence is the same</li></ul><p>By the Gu Chensha / Tang Luo judgment table:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Ye Fan</th><th>Tang Luo</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Uniqueness dependency</td><td>Medium</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Civilization form</td><td>Oligarchic</td><td>Bestowal style</td></tr><tr><td>Predation form</td><td>Patriciate (family private occupation)</td><td>Attachment (personal bestowal)</td></tr><tr><td>Order carrier</td><td>Strong-one group</td><td>One person + embryonic organization</td></tr><tr><td>Corruption path</td><td>Second-generation infighting</td><td>Legacy-favor decay</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Interesting contrast: Ye Fan&#39;s dependency rating (medium) is slightly lower than Tang Luo&#39;s (high), because oligarchic groups have higher fault tolerance than single points; but Ye Fan&#39;s predation depth is actually greater — he wrote order directly into the family name, one step further than Tang Luo&#39;s &quot;temporary trusteeship.&quot;</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Oligarchic / Bestowal</th><th>Anchor Symbiosis Network Style</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ye Fan group co-rule</td><td>Anchor Council open legislation, Myriad Races representatives participate, no patriciates</td></tr><tr><td>Tang Luo one person adjudicates</td><td>Multi-layer separation of powers: legislative/executive/judicial/supervisory four powers separated</td></tr><tr><td>Peace bears the surname Ye</td><td>Myriad Races republican co-building, civilizational dividends distributed by contribution, not by surname</td></tr><tr><td>Brotherhood-style order</td><td>Law-anchored authority benefits all beings, order by law not by relation</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Alternative&#39;s crux: Ye Fan&#39;s problem is &quot;circle too small,&quot; Tang Luo&#39;s problem is &quot;center too bright.&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou solves both problems together — neither circled nor bright, but distributed light.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Ye Fan oligarchic group and Tang Luo single point two models</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: simulate the first generation of strong ones all exiting, observe second and third generations</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: Ye Fan group second-generation infighting probability, Tang Luo group legacy-favor decay rate</li><li><strong>Review conclusion</strong>: Ye Fan group inevitably civil war in the third generation, Tang Luo group institutional vacuum at the end of the second generation — both need network-style alternatives to continue</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Ye Fan system</strong>: setting self-consistency medium (early realm division fine, late Great Emperor/Mortal-World Immortal stage collapses; Wheel Sea, Dao Palace, Four Extremes, Dragon Transformation lose binding force); retcon-ending risk <strong>high</strong> — this is Cover the Sky&#39;s most famous wound: for hot-blooded scenes, early iron rules are broken again and again</li><li><strong>Tang Luo system</strong>: setting self-consistency medium-high; retcon-ending risk medium</li><li><strong>Comparison conclusion</strong>: by retcon-ending, Ye Fan is one tier more severe than Tang Luo. Tang Luo&#39;s risk is &quot;single-point dependency,&quot; Ye Fan&#39;s risk is &quot;realm watering&quot; — two illnesses, same source (law does not come first)</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: oligarchic circles and single-point centers are both civilizational energy mismatches</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: patriciate-style predation is more institutionalized than attachment-style predation, and more tenacious</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo has more openness toward all beings than Ye Fan, but lacks the oligarchic group&#39;s fault tolerance</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: circles and single points both cannot cover 99%</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: cross-plane governance must be anti-patriciate and anti-single-point</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Ye Fan gives all beings ten-thousand-year peace; Tang Luo gives all beings a cultivation road. Both are one step further than Gu Chensha&#39;s &quot;bearing on behalf of all beings,&quot; but neither reaches &quot;letting all beings legislate for themselves.&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s judgment: oligarchic is slightly more stable than single point, bestowal is slightly softer than patriciate — but as long as law does not come first, stability and softness are only procrastination.</p><p>In the final analysis, Tang-Luo · comparison with Ye Fan described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./30-五种共生文明分型总览.html">30-Five Symbiotic Civilization Typology Overview</a> · <a href="./29-共生度评估体系.html">29-Symbiosis Degree Evaluation System</a> · <a href="./17-位面至高强者标准.html">17-Plane Transcendent Standards</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const p=t(a,[["render",s]]);export{u as __pageData,p as default};
